From 9538288cfca2aab0ea476b6f9cece5da6a8ec940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:04:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ask the layout manager's delegate about each line fragment

-layoutManager:shouldSetLineFragmentRect:lineFragmentUsedRect:
baselineOffset:inTextContainer:forGlyphRange:, an NSLayoutManagerDelegate
method since macOS 10.11, lets the delegate change a line fragment's
rect, used rect and baseline offset before they are stored. GNUstep
neither declared nor called it, so a delegate that pads a line had no
effect: an editor that aligns the lines of two texts side by side, say,
where paragraph spacing will not do because the text storage is shared
with other views.

NSLayoutManager.h now declares the NSLayoutManagerDelegate protocol with
this method, optional. GSHorizontalTypesetter asks the delegate before
-setLineFragmentRect:forGlyphRange:usedRect:, passing the fragment's
rect, its used rect and the line's baseline offset: the distance from
the top of the fragment down to the baseline, which is what the
typesetter adds to each glyph's position to get its location in the
fragment. When the delegate answers YES, the rects it returns are
stored and its baseline offset places the fragment's glyphs (and a
truncation glyph), so a larger offset moves them down; the next line
starts below the lowest of the line's fragments as stored, so a taller
fragment pushes every later line down, in its paragraph and the next.
When it answers NO, nothing changes. The extra line fragment after a
trailing newline is not offered to the delegate.

With such a delegate the typesetter no longer reuses soft-invalidated
line fragments after an edit. Reuse shifts the fragments below the edit
as they were stored, the delegate's earlier answer included, without
asking it again, so an answer that changed with the edit would never
take effect. Those lines are laid out again instead and the delegate is
asked about each; a layout manager whose delegate lacks the method
reuses them as before.

Tests/gui/NSLayoutManager/shouldSetLineFragmentRect.m lays out three
paragraphs, the second wrapping, with delegates that add 10 points to
the height of the second paragraph's first fragment: the fragment and
its used rect are 10 points taller, the fragments above are unchanged,
the next line of the paragraph and the next paragraph are 10 points
lower, the glyphs stay at the padded fragment's top unless the baseline
offset grows with it, the proposed offset is the glyphs' height in the
fragment, and an answer of NO changes nothing. After an insertion in
the first line the delegate is asked down to the last glyph again and a
new answer (20 points) is used. On master 13 of its 18 checks fail; with
the patch all pass, and without the change to reuse the two after the
edit fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
